{"chunk_id":"e38679","wall_time_seconds":1.124210375,"exit_code":0,"original_token_count":1124,"output":"{"body":"## Summary\n\n`PgConnection.query` and `PgConnection.stream` send a `CancelRequest` when interrupted work does not drain promptly. The request uses a side connection with no delivery confirmation. A pooler or proxy can delay it long enough for the cancel to hit the next statement on the same PostgreSQL session.\n\nThis keeps the diagnosis and proxy coverage from #8306, but centralizes cancel tracking on the connection and shares one abort-drain path between queries and streams.\n\n## The fix\n\n`drainAborted` gives an interrupted statement 10 ms to reach `ReadyForQuery` before sending a cancel, avoiding unnecessary cancels for buffered results. Once sent, `cancelPending` stays set until the backend reports `57014`.\n\nIf `ReadyForQuery` arrives first, the connection fires its retirement hooks. A pool invalidates the session before another checkout can receive it, while an existing checkout keeps its lease until release. An interrupt sent while the connection is idle retires it immediately because no active statement can confirm the cancel.\n\n`PgPool.use` retains the `Pool.use` fast path when no connection TTL is configured and no session is waiting to be retired. The unpinned multiplexed path never cancels and is unchanged.\n\nA caller that keeps using the same checkout remains exposed to its own late cancel. An unpooled session has no retirement hook or replacement boundary and remains exposed for the rest of its lifetime. Also, `statement_timeout` reports `57014`, so it can be mistaken for confirmation that the cancel arrived.\n\n## Tests\n\n`PgPool.integration.test.ts` has 23 cases covering confirmed and unconfirmed query and stream cancels, replacement through `pool.get` and `pool.use`, held-session behavior, buffered stream drains, late-cancel isolation, and idle interrupts.\n\nThe cancellation fixtures synchronize through advisory locks and proxy gates rather than depending on row-count timing.\n\n## Validation\n\n- all 23 `PgPool.integration.test.ts` cases pass with testcontainers\n- root typecheck and JSDoc checks pass\n- oxlint, dprint, and `git diff --check` pass\n\nCloses EFF-1445\nCloses #8306\n\n","state":"MERGED","title":"fix(sql-pg): retire a session whose CancelRequest may be in flight","url":"https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/pull/8330"}
{"body":"Closes EFF-3927\n\nAcquire the owner permit in a private scope so that waiting for a connection remains cancellable without losing the permit. A cancelled wait closes that scope immediately. A successful pin installs cleanup before cancellation resumes, and releases ownership only after wire cleanup.\n\nThe new in-process test checks that a multiplexed connection accepts another query after a pin wait is cancelled, without first closing the caller's scope. All 566 sql-pg tests passed locally with PostgreSQL integration enabled. Typecheck and lint passed.","state":"OPEN","title":"Keep PostgreSQL connections reusable after interrupted pin acquisition","url":"https://github.com/Effect-TS/effect/pull/10738"}
